# Citation metadata for Undercurrent (https://citation-file-format.github.io/).
# GitHub reads this file to show the "Cite this repository" button.
#
# Keep title, license, keywords and URLs in sync with pyproject.toml.
# `version` and `date-released` are not derived from git tags: update both by
# hand in the release commit before tagging vX.Y.Z.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Undercurrent in your research or software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "Undercurrent"
abstract: >-
  Undercurrent is Wrynx's activation-probing platform for LLM inference:
  production-grade activation probing and inline intervention for LLM
  inference (Hugging Face, vLLM). You declare which activations to capture
  during generation in a YAML spec, run probes against them (single-shot
  classifiers, running trajectory scores), and choose per extraction point
  whether a probe runs inline, where it can intervene and abort generation,
  or async, where it observes out-of-band without blocking the response.
authors:
  - name: "Wrynx"
repository-code: "https://github.com/wrynx/undercurrent"
url: "https://github.com/wrynx/undercurrent"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - undercurrent
  - llm
  - interpretability
  - activation-probing
  - probes
  - ai-safety
  - vllm
  - transformers
  - guardrails
  - mechanistic-interpretability
  - llm-inference
version: "0.1.0"
# PLACEHOLDER: replace with the actual v0.1.0 release date (YYYY-MM-DD) when tagging.
date-released: "2026-10-01"
